    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22wggX35m5FkHWdDhrw8fGm)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` (e22ceda); independent of every other open PR.\n- Touches only `sp-buffers` (+ its doc and a new test file); no other module reads `sp-name`.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks. A later PR that edits `ibuffer-formats` or `nerd-icons-ibuffer-formats` in `sp-buffers` would need to keep `sp-name` instead of `name` (text conflict only).\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`); nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** `.org` files should appear in `ibuffer` by their `#+title`.\n- **How:** a new display column `sp-name` (copy of the built-in `name` column: mouse map, help text, summary, face) that shows the Org title, else the buffer name.\n- **Both format lists** (`ibuffer-formats` and `nerd-icons-ibuffer-formats`) use `sp-name` where they used `name`.\n- **Title lookup is cheap:**\n  - only Org-mode buffers are looked at, and only the first 4000 characters;\n  - the result is cached per buffer on `buffer-chars-modified-tick`, so the text is scanned again only after an edit;\n  - narrowing is ignored; a missing or empty `#+title` falls back to the buffer name.\n- **Option:** `sp-buffers-org-title-in-ibuffer` (default `t`; `nil` lists buffer names again).\n- **Tradeoff, why not rename buffers:**\n  - titles change while you type, and two notes can share one, so renaming would fight Uniquify and `switch-to-buffer` completion;\n  - the column leaves the real buffer name alone, so Popper, the `name` filters and every `buffer-name` caller keep working.\n  - Cost: the title shows only in ibuffer; `C-x b` and the mode line still show the file name.\n- **Unchanged:** filter groups (they match by mode and name), sorting (compares real buffer names, so a title does not change the order), the Filename column still shows the path.\n- Docs: new section \"Org title in the buffer list\" in `sp-buffers.org` (bullets); `.el` re-tangled, `tools/check-tangle.sh` clean after tangle.\n- Tests: `tests/sp-buffers-test.el`, 12 ERT tests pass on Emacs 29.3 (title found, case/indent, missing, empty, non-Org, narrowing, cache follows edits and is reused, option off, real ibuffer listing, formats and groups still present).\n- Not run in a GUI Emacs with `nerd-icons-ibuffer` and the real vault. `when-let*` style only; no CHANGELOG edit (nightly tidy).\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, fish, `~/.config/emacs-modular`, a few notes in `~/notes` open as buffers.\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 445-ibuffer-org-title; git checkout 445-ibuffer-org-title`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/ui -L tests -l ert -l tests/sp-buffers-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 12 pass\n- [ ] Open two notes with a `#+title`, then `C-x C-b`: the Name column shows the titles, in the \"Org\" group, with icons\n- [ ] An Org file without `#+title` still shows its file name; a non-Org buffer (`*scratch*`, a `.el` file) shows its buffer name\n- [ ] Edit the title in a note, `g` in ibuffer: the new title shows\n- [ ] Press `` ` `` to switch to the compact format: titles show there too\n- [ ] Sorting (`,` cycles) and filter groups behave as before; `/ n` (filter by name) still matches the buffer name\n- [ ] Long titles are elided to the column width, not wrapped\n- [ ] `(setq sp-buffers-org-title-in-ibuffer nil)` then `g`: file names are back\n- [ ] Regression: mark (`m`), delete (`d` `x`) and visit (`RET`) a buffer from the list; mouse-1/mouse-2 on a name still mark/visit\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Nothing in the vault is touched.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBgpXYYPJW4Pe6gy7c)_",
